prostt5_3di_cnn.npz
===================

The 3Di prediction head (two convolutional layers) of ProstT5, converted to
numpy by util/convert_prostt5_cnn.py from
https://github.com/mheinzinger/ProstT5/raw/839d839aea349b0e471eb5e6c9f3458ed864019e/cnn_chkpnt/model.pt
(sha256 d2cb4150884de095dac3de81b8fe7842ab1265de41dd5e8c9970879a71e62f3e).
Only the classifier tensors are kept.

The ProstT5 encoder itself is not shipped; learnMSA-3di downloads
Rostlab/ProstT5_fp16 (MIT license) from Hugging Face at a pinned revision.

Citation:
Heinzinger M, Weissenow K, Gomez Sanchez J, Henkel A, Mirdita M,
Steinegger M, Rost B. Bilingual language model for protein sequence and
structure. NAR Genomics and Bioinformatics 6(4), lqae150 (2024).

